# Firebase Functions/Python Coding Rules

## Code Style and Formatting

### General Python Rules

- Follow PEP 8 style guide: https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0008/
- Use 4-space indentation (not tabs)
- Maximum line length: 88 characters (Black formatter default)
- Use snake_case for variables, functions, and methods
- Use PascalCase for classes
- Use UPPER_CASE for constants
- Use descriptive variable names

### Import Organization

- Group imports in this order:
  1. Standard library imports
  2. Third-party imports
  3. Local application imports
- Separate import groups with blank lines
- Use absolute imports when possible
- Avoid wildcard imports (`from module import *`)

### Function and Class Structure

- Keep functions small and focused on a single responsibility
- Use type hints for function parameters and return values
- Add docstrings for all public functions and classes
- Use meaningful function and variable names
- Implement proper error handling

### Error Handling

- Use try-except blocks for operations that might fail
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Log errors appropriately
- Use custom exceptions when needed
- Handle edge cases properly

### Firebase Functions Specific Rules

### Function Structure

- Use proper Firebase Functions decorators (`@functions.https.on_call`, `@functions.https.on_request`, etc.)
- Implement proper authentication checks
- Use rate limiting when appropriate
- Handle CORS properly for HTTP functions
- Implement proper request validation

### Authentication and Authorization

- Always verify user authentication in callable functions
- Check user permissions before performing operations
- Use Firebase Auth tokens for user identification
- Implement proper role-based access control
- Handle unauthenticated requests gracefully

### Firestore Operations

- Use batch operations for multiple writes
- Implement proper transaction handling
- Use proper indexing for queries
- Handle Firestore errors appropriately
- Implement proper data validation

### Security Rules

- Write comprehensive Firestore security rules
- Test security rules thoroughly
- Use proper data validation on both client and server
- Implement proper access control
- Handle sensitive data appropriately

### Performance

- Use connection pooling for external services
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Optimize database queries
- Use async/await properly
- Implement proper timeout handling

### Testing

- Write unit tests for all functions
- Mock external dependencies
- Test error scenarios
- Use proper test fixtures
- Implement integration tests

